SumUp is built with the Godot Engine, which is under the MIT license, with
notices for the parts the engine includes. The About screen shows the full
engine license and every notice, read from the engine itself.

On Android, SumUp also includes libraries that the Godot Engine's Android
build adds: the AndroidX libraries (The Android Open Source Project), the
Kotlin standard library, kotlinx.coroutines and the JetBrains Java
Annotations (JetBrains s.r.o. and contributors), all under the Apache
License, version 2.0, and LLVM libc++ (The LLVM Project contributors), under
the Apache License, version 2.0, with LLVM exceptions. The About screen
lists them with the license text.

